  "raw": {
    "https://www.hlg.edu/job_opening/director-of-athletics/": {
      "title": "Director of Athletics",
      "description": "Director of Athletics | Hannibal-LaGrange University Request info Apply now Give Search for Search Position Number: 1.7 Date: 9/28/2026 Position Title: Director of Athletics Department: Administration Division: Athletics Number of hours per week for which this position is budgeted: 40 Number of months per year for which this position is budgeted: 12 Reports to: President FLSA Classification Grade: Exempt POSITION SUMMARY The Director of Athletics is responsible to the President. The position is full-time and does offer benefits as specified in the employee handbook. The Athletic Director provides institutional leadership in collaborating with key stakeholders at the university to include, but not limited to: students, faculty, staff, alumni, community, corporate sponsors, and donors to forge an ambitious vision for excellence that is compatible with the overall mission and vision to be a Christ centered institution. Employee must possess a vibrant, personal Christian faith including a clear testimony of Christian conversion and be actively involved in a Southern Baptist church. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Promote a culture of Christ-centered, competitive, and academic excellence for student athletes. Provide strategic leadership for the athletics department while maintaining a visible, positive, and energetic presence within the campus community. Accountable for achieving Athletics Department Key Performance Indicators (KPIs), including student-athlete enrollment targets, net revenue goals for each athletic program and the department as a whole, and discount rate goals for each athletic program and the department as a whole; regularly evaluate performance and implement corrective action as necessary to meet institutional objectives Collaborate with appropriate offices on effective enrollment management and scholarship strategies. Understand and embrace the NAIA Champions of Character initiative, fulfilling necessary requirements as an overflow of HLGU as a Christian institution. Responsibly manage and oversee all aspects of the athletics department budget including sound stewardship and fiscal responsibility. Hire, supervise and evaluate all full and part-time employees including coaching and administrative staff. Determine and administer employee work assignments such as coaching and non instructional duties Represent HLGU at American Midwest Conference and NAIA National Meetings. Act as a Campus Security Authority (CSA) DEPARTMENTAL RELATIONSHIPS Support the strategic plan of the university while collaborating with, but not limited to, the following departments: Registrar Office and Financial Aid Office, Faculty Athletic Representative, Academic Dean, Director of Admissions, Public Relations, and Human Resources. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Must have values consistent with the mission and purpose of Hannibal-LaGrange University. • Must agree to, sign off on, and abide by the standards of employment on the back of the application, on the yearly contract, and in the staff handbook. Ability to apply budgetary and fiscal planning techniques within financial constraints. • Ability to provide administrative guidance within area of responsibility, providing direct training and supervision as needed. Strong skills in verbal and written communication, organization, multi-tasking, efficiency, and customer service. Ability to work with a diverse constituency including students, parents, coaches, faculty, staff, administrators and outside contacts. Previous experience preferred in administration or other leadership position. • Must be proficient in computer applications such as Microsoft Word and Outlook. EDUCATION, EXPERIENCE, AND TRAINING Bachelor’s Degree required, Master’s Degree preferred. 3-5 years of demonstrated leadership experience required; success at the collegiate level preferred. Working knowledge and application of NAIA eligibility standards, rules, and regulations. To apply, please submit an application, including a cover here. Disclaimer * This job description is not intended to be all-inclusive; an employee will also perform other reasonably related job responsibilities as assigned by immediate supervisor and/or other management as required. HLGU reserves the right to revise or change job duties, required skills, or qualifications as the need arises. This job description does not constitute a written or implied contract of employment. The aforementioned job requirements are subject to change to reasonably accommodate qualified disabled individuals."
    },
    "https://www.hlg.edu/job_opening/marketing-and-communications-coordinator/": {
      "title": "Marketing and Communications Coordinator",
      "description": "Marketing and Communications Coordinator | Hannibal-LaGrange University Request info Apply now Give Search for Search Position Number: 1.4.2.1 Date : April 27, 2026 Position Title: Marketing and Communications Coordinator Department: Marketing Division: Institutional Advancement Number of hours per week for which this position is budgeted: 40 Number of months per year for which this position is budgeted: 12 Reports to: Vice President for Institutional Advancement Grade: Exempt POSITION SUMMARY The Marketing and Communication Coordinator plays a key role in advancing the University’s brand and strategic messaging across digital and traditional platforms. This position is responsible for supporting the execution of the HLGU marketing strategy that supports student recruitment, alumni and friends’ engagement, and institutional visibility. The ideal candidate will possess strong skills in social media management, website management, videography, graphic design, and photography. Employee must possess a vibrant, personal Christian faith including a clear testimony of Christian conversion and be actively involved in an evangelical, preferably Southern Baptist, church. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Key Responsibilities: Assist with the execution of university-wide marketing and communication plans. • Coordinate campaigns that align with institutional goals and target audiences. • Monitor and analyze campaign performance metrics to optimize future efforts. • Monitor and manage the HLGU website. Work with departments and our website specialist to make updates and improvements to ensure branding and message. Digital & Social Media Management o Manage the university’s social media accounts (Instagram, Facebook, Twitter, Linkedln, YouTube, etc.). o Create engaging content tailored to each platform, including graphics, videos, and written posts along with Social Media Specialist. o Track engagement and trends to inform content strategy. Content Creation o Capture high-quality photos and videos for use in marketing materials, social media, and the university website. o Edit and produce short-form and long-form video content for promotional and informational purposes. o Maintain a digital asset library of multimedia content. o Create graphics for marketing materials, social media, and the university website. Brand Stewardship o Ensure consistency in messaging and visual identity across all communications. o Collaborate with departments and faculty to support their marketing needs while maintaining brand standards. . Event Support o Provide marketing support for university events, including marketing plans, promotional materials, live coverage, and post-event recaps. o Document events through photography and videography. DEPARTMENTAL RELATIONSHIPS The position of Marketing and Communications Coordinator requires a working relationship with all departments on campus, working closely with the Executive Cabinet to communicate to both internal and external audiences. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Must possess excellent leadership skills. Must be able to effectively plan and meet multiple deadlines and high-pressure timetables. • Must possess good initiative and the ability to work without close supervision. • Must demonstrate excellent organizational and prioritization skills. Requires the highest level of relational skills in working with University personnel to meet their needs, and in working with outside vendors. Must be creative and have excellent communication skills. Must be a team player who has the good of the organization at heart. Must have values consistent with the mission and purpose of Hannibal-LaGrange University. Must agree to, sign off on, and abide by the standards of employment on the employment application, on the yearly contract, and in the employee handbook. EDUCATION, EXPERIENCE, AND TRAINING Bachelor’s degree in Marketing, Communications, Media Studies, or a related field. 2+ years of experience in marketing, communications, or digital media. Proficiency in social media platforms and scheduling tools (e.g., Hootsuite, Buffer). • Strong photography and videography skills, including editing software (e.g., Adobe Premiere Pro, Final Cut Pro, Lightroom). Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Ability to manage multiple projects and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment. • Familiarity with higher education marketing is a plus. Experience with content management systems (e.g., WordPress). Graphic design skills using tools like Canva or Adobe Creative Suite. Knowledge of SEO and digital advertising strategies. An aptitude for utilizing a team approach to accomplish goals and objectives in an environment of divergent views and opinions. Can express a mature Christian testimony and communicate and support the merits of a Christian education. Preference will be given to Hannibal-LaGrange University graduates. To apply, please submit an application, including a cover here. Disclaimer * This job description is not intended to be all-inclusive; an employee will also perform other reasonably related job responsibilities as assigned by immediate supervisor and/or other management as required. HLGU reserves the right to revise or change job duties, required skills, or qualifications as the need arises. This job description does not constitute a written or implied contract of employment. The aforementioned job requirements are subject to change to reasonably accommodate qualified disabled individuals."
    },
    "https://www.hlg.edu/job_opening/maintenance-worker-2/": {
      "title": "Maintenance Worker",
      "description": "Maintenance Worker | Hannibal-LaGrange University Request info Apply now Give Search for Search Position Number: 1.3.1.2. Date: 06/16/2026 Position Title: Maintenance Worker Department: Maintenance Division: Campus Operations Number of hours per week for which this position is budgeted: 40 Number of months per year for which this position is budgeted: 12 Reports to: Director of Campus Operations FLSA Grade: Non-Exempt POSITION SUMMARY The Maintenance Worker reports to the Director of Campus Operations. The position is full-time and offers benefits as outlined in the Employee Handbook. Employee must possess a vibrant, personal Christian faith including a clear testimony of Christian conversion and be actively involved in an evangelical, preferably Southern Baptist, church. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Carpentry Plumbing Electrical Heating and air conditioning Cleanup of construction debris Snow removal Room set up for college and community activities Vehicle cleaning and repair KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Must demonstrate proficiency in at least one area of maintenance including but not limited to: HVAC Carpentry Electrical Plumbing Locksmithing Welding Metal fabrication Auto mechanics Small engine repair Additionally, must be able to lift up to 60 lbs and be comfortable working at heights up to 50 feet. EDUCATION, EXPERIENCE, AND TRAINING High school diploma or equivalency required One year of Maintenance experience To apply, please submit an application, including a cover here. Disclaimer * This job description is not intended to be all-inclusive; an employee will also perform other reasonably related job responsibilities as assigned by immediate supervisor and/or other management as required. HLGU reserves the right to revise or change job duties, required skills, or qualifications as the need arises. This job description does not constitute a written or implied contract of employment. The aforementioned job requirements are subject to change to reasonably accommodate qualified disabled individuals."
    },
    "https://www.hlg.edu/job_opening/jefferson-city-correctional-center-jccc-program-ministry-assistant/": {
      "title": "Jefferson City Correctional Center (JCCC) Program Ministry Assistant",
      "description": "Jefferson City Correctional Center (JCCC) Program Ministry Assistant | Hannibal-LaGrange University Request info Apply now Give Search for Search Position Number: 1.2.5.4.3 Date: September 16, 2025 Position Title: Jefferson City Correctional Center (JCCC) Program Ministry Assistant Department: Academic Administration Division: Academic Administration Number of hours per week for which this position is budgeted: 40 Number of months per year for which this position is budgeted: 12 Reports to: Vice President for Academic Administration Grade: Exempt ☐ Non-Exempt ☒ POSITION SUMMARY This position is responsible to the Vice President for Academic Administration (VPAA). The position is full-time and offers benefits as specified in the staff handbook. The Ministry Assistant provides direct administrative support for the JCCC Program staff and faculty, supervises tier-walking groups, and conducts pastoral counseling to students. Employee must possess a vibrant, personal Christian faith including a clear testimony of Christian conversion and be actively involved in an evangelical, preferably Southern Baptist, church. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Maintain Faculty, Participant, and Program Academic Records Administer Equipment Servicing and Repair Order Supplies and Textbooks Effectively communicate with participants, donors, outside academic institutions, and other external partners. Transport supplies between the HLGU main campus and JCCC as needed. Other duties as assigned (including but not limited to). Setup and participate in convocation, graduation and other special events Shepherding Tier-Walking groups Program support projects as assigned by the Director DEPARTMENTAL RELATIONSHIPS This position requires a working relationship with all departments on the main campus and at the JCCC location. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES This position requires the ability to work in a fast-paced environment. Strong organizational skills and the ability to prioritize are necessary. This position requires a general understanding of academic programs and higher education as well as Christian ministry. This position requires the ability to relate to others at all times with courtesy and diplomacy. Light lifting (up to 40 lbs.) in an office setting is required. Must have values consistent with the mission and purpose of Hannibal-LaGrange University. Must agree to, sign off on, and abide by the standards of employment in the staff handbook. EDUCATION, EXPERIENCE, AND TRAINING A bachelor’s degree is required; a Master’s degree is preferred. Experience with Christian based ministry and counseling services. Experience in an office management or other position requiring position is preferred. Proficiency and professionalism in oral, written and electronic office communications. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite, especially Word, Excel, PowerPoint. Experience with MS Access is helpful. To apply, please submit an application, including a cover here. Disclaimer * This job description is not intended to be all-inclusive; an employee will also perform other reasonably related job responsibilities as assigned by immediate supervisor and/or other management as required. HLGU reserves the right to revise or change job duties, required skills, or qualifications as the need arises. This job description does not constitute a written or implied contract of employment. The aforementioned job requirements are subject to change to reasonably accommodate qualified disabled individuals."
    },
    "https://www.hlg.edu/job_opening/graduate-assistant-mens-ministry/": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant – Men’s Ministry",
      "description": "Graduate Assistant – Men’s Ministry | Hannibal-LaGrange University Request info Apply now Give Search for Search Position Number: 1.6.6.1 Date: 07/02/2026 Position Title: Graduate Assistant – Men’s Ministry Department: Student Life/Campus Ministries Division: Student Life Number of hours per week for which this position is budgeted: 20 Number of months per year for which this position is budgeted: 12 Reports to: Dean of Students & Campus Chaplain Exempt: Non-Exempt: X POSITION SUMMARY The Graduate Assistant for Men’s Ministry serves within the Office of Student Life to advance the spiritual formation of male students at Hannibal-LaGrange University. This role focuses on cultivating Christ-centered discipleship, strengthening engagement in campus worship, and mobilizing students for evangelism and missions. The GA will work closely with the Dean of Students & Campus Chaplain to foster a culture of biblical discipleship aligned with the Baptist Faith & Message and the mission of HLGU. Employee must possess a vibrant, personal Christian faith including a clear testimony of Christian conversion and be actively involved in an evangelical, preferably Southern Baptist, church. PRIMARY RESPONSIBILITIES Men’s Discipleship Develop and lead intentional discipleship initiatives for male students (small groups, one-on-one mentoring, accountability structures) Recruit, train, and support student leaders to disciple their peers Promote spiritual habits such as Scripture reading, prayer, and gospel-centered community Assist in identifying and shepherding emerging male student leaders Campus Worship Support planning and execution of weekly chapel services with a focus on meaningful engagement of male students Collaborate with worship teams and student leaders to encourage participation from male students in worship leadership Assist in developing worship environments that prioritize congregational participation and theological soundness Missions & Evangelism Help organize and promote campus evangelism initiatives Equip male students to share the gospel faithfully and confidently Assist with local church partnerships, service projects, and mission opportunities Support the development and coordination of student mission teams and outreach efforts ADDITIONAL DUTIES Participate in Student Life team meetings and campus ministry planning Assist with campus-wide spiritual formation events (revivals, retreats, special services) Provide general support for Student Life initiatives as assigned Maintain regular office hours and consistent availability to students QUALIFICATIONS Admission to an HLGU graduate program (required) Strong commitment to Jesus Christ and agreement with the Baptist Faith & Message Demonstrated involvement in local church ministry Experience in discipleship, student leadership, or ministry preferred Strong interpersonal, organizational, and leadership skills EXPECTATIONS Maintain active membership and involvement in a local Southern Baptist or like-minded church Model Christian character, integrity, and spiritual maturity Be relationally engaged and visible among students, especially male students Uphold and support the mission and values of Hannibal-LaGrange University TERMS OF EMPLOYMENT 2-3 year commitment required, depending on academic program chosen Tuition Concession for 6 credit hours of graduate course work per semester (fall, spring, summer) $500 monthly stipend + free on-campus housing (if available) Practical ministry experience in a collegiate context APPLICATION PROCESS Interested candidates should submit: Resume Statement of faith and testimony Ministry philosophy (brief) References (including a pastoral reference) To apply, please submit an application, including a cover here. Disclaimer * This job description is not intended to be all-inclusive; an employee will also perform other reasonably related job responsibilities as assigned by immediate supervisor and/or other management as required. HLGU reserves the right to revise or change job duties, required skills, or qualifications as the need arises. This job description does not constitute a written or implied contract of employment. The aforementioned job requirements are subject to change to reasonably accommodate qualified disabled individuals."
    },
